preConditionHook:
// HigherSwingLowRun -- Grimes A list, keys HigherSwingLowRun (G06-43) and
// RisingSwingLowCount (G05-07). Authored 2026-09-22 as a `legs` input on
// HigherSwingLow and split out as its own rule 2026-11-07, because the 202611
// BRK and OWN templates place HigherSwingLow, so HigherSwingLow stays exactly
// as those families run it. Code otherwise unchanged. The default legs(3) is
// Grimes's reading and both merged keys' own number.
//
// A RUN OF HIGHER LOWS: each of the last `legs` CONFIRMED swing lows is above
// the one before it. Grimes reads the run as pullbacks getting shallower into
// a level, his ascending-triangle accumulation, at legs 3 (G05-07, G06-43). At
// legs 2 it is Brooks's minimum precondition for a with-trend trade, "a trader
// usually should not be looking to buy unless the market is at least forming a
// higher low". Mirrored: the short side wants the last `legs` swing HIGHS each
// below the one before, a run of lower highs.
//
// TWO merged keys proposed this input -- HigherSwingLowRun's `legs` and
// RisingSwingLowCount's `minRisingLows` -- and they are ONE INPUT, not two:
// both ask for the same chain of pairwise comparisons over the same
// newest-first pivot scan. `legs` is the name kept. The count of COMPARISONS
// is `legs` - 1, so legs 2 is one comparison and legs 3 is two.
// RisingSwingLowCount's ascending-triangle second half -- a flat ceiling while
// the lows rise -- is LevelTouchCount or Ledge in its own pane, not folded in.
//
// AT legs 2 THIS IS HigherSwingLow's BEHAVIOUR BUT NOT ITS TEXT: the run
// reduces to occurrences 1 and 2 and the single comparison between them, but
// both twins spell the scan differently -- here one loop serves both sides and
// runs without a break, and the EL twin inlines the scan where HigherSwingLow
// calls SwingLow / SwingLowBar / SwingHigh / SwingHighBar.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED IN BOTH TWINS. It has to be: the register's
// swinghigh / swinglow / swinghighbar / swinglowbar rows are VERIFIED but list
// Occurrence 3+ explicitly as UNMEASURED, and legs 3 needs a third pivot. The
// inlined scan is the route TrendLineSlopeFlattening ratified for a third or
// later pivot, since plain EL loops and comparisons are registered and the scan
// reproduces the MEASURED pivot test exactly.
//
// MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min):
//   * the pivot test is MIXED: at-or-beyond the `strength` OLDER bars, STRICTLY
//     beyond the `strength` NEWER bars. Bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER
//     index the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the kk < jj loop;
//   * the confirmation lag is exactly `strength` bars, never 0 or 1, so the
//     scan is lookahead-safe, and during the lag it reports the PREVIOUS pivot;
//   * maxBarsBack is EL's Length: candidate offsets 0..maxBarsBack-1 from the
//     current bar INCLUSIVE, and the neighbourhood test reaches `strength` bars
//     PAST the window, so the deepest bar touched is
//     maxBarsBack - 1 + strength;
//   * fewer than `legs` pivots in the window is the -1 SENTINEL case, guarded
//     here by the COUNT reaching `legs` -- never by a price test, because -1 and
//     0 are legitimate prices in a back-adjusted series;
//   * the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance;
//   * the low side's tie sense is the mirror of the measured high-side rule,
//     not an observation. No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs.
//
// THE RUN IS TESTED AS THE SCAN GOES, one comparison per newly found pivot
// against the previous one, so no array and no numbered pivot slots are needed
// and `legs` is unbounded above. loPrev / hiPrev are only ever READ once the
// count has reached 2, which is exactly when they were written earlier on the
// same bar -- they are never a sentinel and never a stale price.
//
// Not LaggedHigherHigh, which compares two ADJACENT BARS at a fixed lag on the
// opposite series, and not HigherLowCount, which counts adjacent-bar pairs.
// This reads the STRUCTURE -- confirmed pivots, however many bars apart --
// which no fixed-lag bar comparison reaches. The cheap window proxy the merge
// recorded (lowest(low, n) now against lowest(low, n) n bars ago) is a
// different test and is not used. Not TrendingHighsAndLows or StairsPattern.
//
// The loops run WITHOUT a break -- EasyLanguage has no loop break -- and the
// `nLo < legs` guard is what stops a later pivot being folded into the run.
//
// Deepest bar touched: maxBarsBack - 1 + strength.
//
// Every scratch value that must survive the bar is a localVariables entry; the
// loop counters and the per-candidate flags are declared inside braced blocks,
// which are block-scoped and so safe under a double placement (the
// AwesomeOscillatorSlope / TrendLineSlopeFlattening precedent).
nLo = 0;
nHi = 0;
loOk = true;
hiOk = true;
loPrev = 0.0;
hiPrev = 0.0;
for (int jj = (int)strength; jj <= (int)maxBarsBack - 1; ++jj) {
    bool okLo = true;
    bool okHi = true;
    for (int kk = jj - (int)strength; kk < jj; ++kk) {
        if (el_ge(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
        if (el_le(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
    }
    for (int kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + (int)strength; ++kk) {
        if (el_gt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
        if (el_lt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
    }
    if (okLo && nLo < (int)legs) {
        nLo = nLo + 1;
        if (nLo >= 2 && el_le(loPrev, low[jj])) loOk = false;
        loPrev = low[jj];
    }
    if (okHi && nHi < (int)legs) {
        nHi = nHi + 1;
        if (nHi >= 2 && el_ge(hiPrev, high[jj])) hiOk = false;
        hiPrev = high[jj];
    }
}
haveLo = nLo >= (int)legs;
haveHi = nHi >= (int)legs;
